{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matrixorigin/matrixone/pulls/29861","id":4816099800,"node_id":"PR_kwDOFEPiGM8AAAABHw_Z2A","html_url":"https://github.com/matrixorigin/matrixone/pull/29861","diff_url":"https://github.com/matrixorigin/matrixone/pull/29861.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/matrixorigin/matrixone/pull/29861.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matrixorigin/matrixone/issues/29861","number":29861,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix: validate identifier encoding and preserve legacy catalog keys","user":{"login":"XuPeng-SH","id":39627130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NjI3MTMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39627130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/XuPeng-SH","html_url":"https://github.com/XuPeng-SH","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XuPeng-SH/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XuPeng-SH/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XuPeng-SH/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XuPeng-SH/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XuPeng-SH/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XuPeng-SH/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XuPeng-SH/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XuPeng-SH/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XuPeng-SH/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What type of PR is this?\n\n- [x] BUG\n\n## Which issue(s) this PR fixes:\n\nFixes #29843\nFixes #29864\nFixes #29874\n\n## What this PR does / why we need it:\n\nMalformed UTF-8 identifiers could be admitted into the catalog. Catalog lookups formatted their names with Go `%q`, whose `\\xNN` escapes are not decoded as hex by the MySQL scanner. A legacy `t_\\xe3g` lookup therefore used `t_xe3g`; DROP DATABASE hit the missing-row cardinality panic.\n\n- Extend the existing DDL identifier validator to reject malformed UTF-8 before publication. Check original CTAS/view headings before normalization, cover CREATE SEQUENCE with encoding-only validation while preserving historically supported long sequence names, and keep generated/internal table exceptions restricted to identifier length.\n- Use the existing `sqlquote.String` helper at every consumer of the seven name-bearing catalog query formats. Lookup, storage fallback, enumeration and deletion retain exact legacy bytes, tenant predicates, table IDs and existing result ownership/cardinality checks.\n- Preserve raw-byte parsing for legacy object access and string/binary values. Validation targets names published by DDL; ordinary SELECT alias semantics are unchanged. No new validation runs on ordinary SELECT/DML. Additional scans run during DDL validation; quoting changes existing catalog SQL construction and preserve name-based pruning. No new persistent format, state or executor.\n\n- Reuse main’s #29866 and #29873 idxcron fixes: retain existing command/status escaping, scalar COUNT existence handling and the complete account/table/index/action status key. Consolidate new error-precedence, owned-result cleanup and exact write-error checks into the existing status test. Add command byte round trips and actual public vector-index lifecycle isolation coverage; remove unconditional raw SQL stderr writes.\n- Correct the shared `mo_indexes` deletion format and both DROP INDEX / ALTER TABLE DROP INDEX consumers together. Legal quoted index names now delete the intended metadata and maintenance task while preserving competing indexes and table data. No new builder, algorithm branch, schema or scheduler.\n\n### Validation\n\nOn Linux amd64, Go 1.27.1, with a freshly built/stamped CPU CGo generation:\n\n- Reproduced the original admission and DROP DATABASE panic through the actual MySQL protocol on base `4022729da24d71b082c22b52aaed3faba2b77ea5`.\n- Public protocol regression: malformed CREATE/CTAS/view rejected before metadata appears; legal Unicode, quoted/backslash names and binary prepared parameters preserved. Seeded historical invalid table/database names through the real typed engine interface, then verified DROP TABLE and DROP DATABASE without deleting competing `t_xe3g`/replacement-character tables.\n- Incremental UT **with `-race`**: existing and new identifier tests; full catalog and MySQL parser packages; actual storage query round trips; existing result ownership/read failure/cancel/cardinality, catalog replay/GC and temporary-schema tests; `TestApplyDeletesFromTombstoneObjects` directly affected consumer.\n- Incremental SCA on all affected packages: `go vet`, repository-configured golangci-lint v2.14.0 (**0 new issues**) and pinned molint. Molint's existing recover/unsafe diagnostics are confined to files byte-identical to base; no new findings.\n- Sequence compatibility correction: planner owning package normal (15.586s) and race (92.755s), public catalog regression normal/race, configured incremental lint **0 issues**, and molint without introduced findings. Original sequence case passed twice (**167/167** each); complete sequence directory passed **461/461** in normal comparison mode. Seven ASCII/Unicode/long-name lifecycle controls and short/long malformed-name rejection verified through SQL. Local BVT used one CN; corrected Compose/PROXY CI is pending.\n- New idxcron/index deletion closure: full idxcron and compile owning packages in normal and race modes; scanner and JSON round trips, error precedence/propagation and result release. Configured incremental SCA covers idxcron, compile and embed; no introduced findings (molint's recover diagnostics are in unchanged baseline files).\n- Actual MySQL-protocol regression with three databases and three vector rows per table: exact registration names, rejected rename without task changes, two quoted-name renames with stable table IDs/data/metadata, disable/re-enable configuration, backslash-name DROP DATABASE isolation, DROP INDEX and ALTER TABLE DROP INDEX preserving same-table competing indexes/tasks and data, and explicit zero catalog/task residue. Normal and two race executions using the same shared fixture passed.\n- Actual `gpt-6.1-sol / xhigh` design and complete 14-file final review; its missing final task-cleanup oracle was added and revalidated before delivery.\n\n### Compatibility\n\nHistorical malformed names remain readable/deletable; creating or renaming to a new malformed name is rejected. This does not sanitize existing catalogs. Admission protection requires upgrading every CN that can author DDL. This does not backfill already corrupted maintenance-task keys: re-registration replaces a row only when its account/table/index/action key matches. CI for the pushed revision is pending.\n","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:45:29Z","updated_at":"2026-10-11T10:05:03Z","closed_at":"2026-10-11T10:04:59Z","merged_at":"2026-10-11T10:04:59Z","merge_commit_sha":"e454407a1a94d13fd136706d02ffb5f0dfa3de35","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"fengttt","id":169294,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2OTI5NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169294?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fengttt","html_url":"https://github.com/fengttt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fengttt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fengttt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fengttt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fengttt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fengttt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fengttt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fengttt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fengttt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fengttt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"aunjgr","id":523063,"node_